            <ArticleTitle>Breakpoint: left main stent fracture--review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>362-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8183.2009.00484.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The incidence and morbidity associated with stent fracture are unknown. Recommendations and evidence-based treatment are lacking. We report a case of symptomatic fracture of a sirolimus-eluting stent advancing from the left main into the circumflex coronary artery, forming an acute angle with calcifications at the hinge point; the literature is reviewed and treatment options are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
